the factor (3 / (4 pi)) pi^(-1/3) = 0.1630; the part of D that is the count of points, (4/9) alpha^2 = 0.781; three quarters of it 0.586
the count itself by (1): (3/4) x 1.3259 x (n / pi)^(2/3) = 99879 at n = 10^8 (the discs: 99,880)
D = 1.073, as measured: the variance of the count should be 0.0794 n^(1/3) for clouds of exactly n points (0.0824 with the measured 0.757 for the count's part), and 0.1749 n^(1/3) if the number of points were left to chance
D = 1.081, with the two small corrections: the variance of the count should be 0.0807 n^(1/3) for clouds of exactly n points (0.0837 with the measured 0.757 for the count's part), and 0.1762 n^(1/3) if the number of points were left to chance

