weighing each size by its number of clouds, the variance over n^(1/3) is 0.0812; predicted 0.0794. (D is good to about 0.06, one standard error, from the resampling of study.out; so the prediction to about 0.010, 12 in 100.)
if the prediction were exact, the scatter of the 9 sizes about it would have a chi-square of 8.5 on 9
